1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,200
Two Hands.

2
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:04,117
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

3
00:00:04,167 --> 00:00:06,200
OCR reads the number.

4
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,950
Two Hands checks whether the whole form agrees.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,283
Mexico counts every tally sheet twice:

6
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:17,569
a fast preliminary capture, then the certified count.

7
00:00:17,619 --> 00:00:21,855
On 6.5% of the polling stations not recounted,

8
00:00:21,905 --> 00:00:26,617
the two official records of the same paper disagree.

9
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:31,855
And 19.2% of national forms fail their own row sum,

10
00:00:31,905 --> 00:00:34,236
in the official capture.

11
00:00:34,286 --> 00:00:39,950
A sum says something is wrong; the photo says which field.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,354
Gemma, on AMD, reads every field twice:

13
00:00:43,404 --> 00:00:46,759
the digits and the amount in words.

14
00:00:46,809 --> 00:00:49,737
A second, independent reader must agree.

15
00:00:49,787 --> 00:00:53,141
The referee is the paper's own arithmetic.

16
00:00:53,191 --> 00:00:55,269
Every check holds: accepted.

17
00:00:55,319 --> 00:00:59,950
One fails: a person sees the field, with its photo.

18
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,950
Here is a real sheet.

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,450
Gemma read 23, in digits and in words.

20
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,950
But the rows sum to 366, not 466.

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,950
On the site, the same sheet: routed to a person.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,950
The paper says 123, and with it the sum holds.

23
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,807
Every field gets a receipt.

24
00:01:26,857 --> 00:01:30,617
Verified: it proves the record is unchanged.

25
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:33,950
Not that the reading is right.

26
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,236
Now a live read.

27
00:01:36,286 --> 00:01:40,807
One request to Gemma, on the AMD Token Factory.

28
00:01:40,857 --> 00:01:45,379
We cut the wait; the timer stays on screen.

29
00:01:45,429 --> 00:01:47,664
It took 90 seconds.

30
00:01:47,714 --> 00:01:49,950
Every check holds: accepted.

31
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,495
This is the product.

32
00:01:52,545 --> 00:01:57,586
An auditor brings the typed data and the scans.

33
00:01:57,636 --> 00:02:02,168
Here, the sample: 6,000 fields, checked in seconds.

34
00:02:02,218 --> 00:02:04,714
267 disputes, strongest first.

35
00:02:04,764 --> 00:02:10,314
This one: the capture keyed 75; the paper says 175.

36
00:02:10,364 --> 00:02:13,877
One fingerprint seals the whole report.

37
00:02:13,927 --> 00:02:17,950
Change one number, and the check fails.

38
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:19,450
The proof.

39
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:24,450
Gemma on AMD read 1,270 real handwritten tally sheets.

40
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,950
49 capture errors, confirmed by the certified count.

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,450
Recall: 27 of 28 capture errors the certified count reveals,

42
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,950
in one state, pre-registered.

43
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,950
A person re-read the AI-judged disputes blind:

44
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,950
0 read differently.

45
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,719
On Baja California Sur's local actas: 91.6% field match.

46
00:02:48,769 --> 00:02:53,912
The Google Document AI reading the state bought

47
00:02:53,962 --> 00:02:57,950
scored 62.84%, on the same metric.

48
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:01,250
Same 300 forms, same gate.

49
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:08,400
It accepts 1.8x the forms Qwen does, at the same error rate,

50
00:03:08,450 --> 00:03:11,150
4.6x cheaper, 2.8x faster.

51
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,900
A whole state: Colima.

52
00:03:13,950 --> 00:03:19,950
Gemma on AMD read all 982 sheets for 14 cents.

53
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,041
Each strong finding becomes a case in Evolus.

54
00:03:24,091 --> 00:03:29,041
The agent runs on Gemma, on AMD, and drafts it.

55
00:03:29,091 --> 00:03:33,132
A script, not the model, scores the evidence.

56
00:03:33,182 --> 00:03:34,950
The auditor decides.

57
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,662
Who pays? Mexico's preliminary counts:

58
00:03:37,712 --> 00:03:41,731
INE, 32 state institutes, and their outside auditors.

59
00:03:41,781 --> 00:03:47,155
On 6 June 2027, 32 local elections join the federal midterm.

60
00:03:47,205 --> 00:03:49,868
$1 per sheet audited, proposed.

61
00:03:49,918 --> 00:03:55,292
The first step: a paid shadow-mode pilot on one state's count.

62
00:03:55,342 --> 00:03:58,909
Next: 7 more countries publish these sheets,

63
00:03:58,959 --> 00:04:03,429
and health reporting in 70+ countries runs on DHIS2.

64
00:04:03,479 --> 00:04:07,950
Elections are our proof set, not our only market.

65
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,950
Where it breaks.

66
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,450
On 100 fresh forms, the model read 3114

67
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,450
where the paper says 314.

68
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,450
No sum covers that field.

69
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:26,450
Gate version two needs the digits and the words to agree,

70
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:29,950
so it went to a person.

71
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,117
Every number re-derives from public data, with one command.

72
00:04:34,167 --> 00:04:35,367
Two Hands.

73
00:04:35,417 --> 00:04:38,283
Verifiable quality control for handwritten numbers.

74
00:04:38,333 --> 00:04:39,950
Running on AMD.
